An empty directory, mounted at /etc/claudio/nginx.d when the operator has no
additions of their own.

Compose cannot mount "nothing", and a bind mount whose source does not exist is
created by the daemon as a root-owned directory -- which the proxy runs as
65534 and cannot read.  So the empty case is a real, committed, empty
directory, and CLAUDIO_NGINX_D replaces it with yours.

Two globs are read from here and they are disjoint by name:

  http-*.conf     included at http level.  A whole `server { }` goes here --
                  a redirect, a second vhost, your own TLS terminator.
  server-*.conf   included INSIDE the plain 8080 server block, next to the
                  routes.  A `location` goes here.

One glob for both would try to include a whole `server { }` inside another one.
